---
sequenceDiagram
    box rgb(224,237,215) Opponent
    participant W as White player
    end
    box rgb(241,245,249) Game controller
    participant L as Lucas Chess
    end
    box rgb(219,232,251) UCI engine
    participant R as Remus (Black)
    end
    Note over W,R: Legal game: 1. f3 e5 2. g4 Qh4 (checkmate), 0-1.<br/>Teaching example, setup complete, Ponder enabled.
    W->>L: Play 1. f3
    L->>L: Update board, switch from White's clock to Black's
    L->>R: position startpos moves f2f3
    L->>R: go wtime 59000 btime 60000 winc 0 binc 0
    R-->>L: bestmove e7e5 ponder g2g4
    L->>L: Play 1...e5, switch clocks
    L-->>W: Show Black's e5, White to move
    L->>R: position startpos moves f2f3 e7e5 g2g4
    L->>R: go ponder wtime 59000 btime 59000 winc 0 binc 0
    Note over L,R: g2g4 is hypothetical in Remus only. Lucas's real board has just 1. f3 e5.
    R->>R: Find 2...Qh4 (checkmate)<br/>Wait for hit or stop
    W->>L: Play the predicted 2. g4
    L->>L: Update real board, start Black's clock
    Note over L,R: Lucas stop-and-go handoff on a correct prediction
    L->>R: stop
    R-->>L: bestmove d8h4
    Note over L,R: This result closes the ponder request. Lucas does not play it yet.
    L->>R: position startpos moves f2f3 e7e5 g2g4
    L->>R: go wtime 57000 btime 59000 winc 0 binc 0
    R->>R: Recognize matching native credit<br/>Recover completed work within time limits
    R-->>L: bestmove d8h4
    L->>L: Play 2...Qh4 (checkmate)<br/>Stop both clocks
    L-->>W: Display 0-1 and final board
    Note over L,R: Lucas manages the game result.<br/>No standard UCI gameover message is required.
    L->>R: quit
    Note right of R: Process exits, no quitok reply
    L->>L: Retain game record and update results
    L-->>W: Show result, review controls, or tournament standings
